ng_ubt: publish each controller as an IOBluetoothHostController entry

bluetoothd has to learn about USB Bluetooth controllers from a kernel
notification, the way wland learns about radios from IO80211Controller.
The bare "ubt" newbus node is a FreeBSD driver name and exists before
the controller is usable, and polling netgraph (NGM_LISTNODES) races
arrival.

Publish a virtual IORegistry entry of class IOBluetoothHostController
under the controller's ubtN node at the end of a successful
ubt_attach(), once the netgraph node is named and the USB transfers are
set up, and retire it at the start of ubt_detach(), before the netgraph
node is torn down. bluetoothd matches it with
IOServiceAddMatchingNotification (first-match and terminated), as
Darwin's bluetoothd follows IOBluetoothHostController. The entry itself
is built in ng_ubt_ioreg.c (this directory's src/), with the kernel's
ioreg_publish_virtual() and ioreg_retire_virtual().

A part still in firmware bootloader mode is refused by ng_ubt's probe,
so it publishes nothing until its firmware is loaded and it
re-enumerates.

Origin: NextBSD (nextbsd/nextbsd-kernel-extensions#27). Not upstream.
Applies to: releng/15.1 sys/netgraph/bluetooth/drivers/ubt/ng_ubt.c

--- a/sys/netgraph/bluetooth/drivers/ubt/ng_ubt.c
+++ b/sys/netgraph/bluetooth/drivers/ubt/ng_ubt.c
@@ -132,6 +132,12 @@
 #include <netgraph/bluetooth/include/ng_ubt.h>
 #include <netgraph/bluetooth/drivers/ubt/ng_ubt_var.h>
 
+/*
+ * NextBSD: IOBluetoothHostController registry entries
+ * (nextbsd-kernel-extensions#27).
+ */
+#include "ng_ubt_ioreg.h"
+
 static int		ubt_modevent(module_t, int, void *);
 static device_probe_t	ubt_probe;
 static device_attach_t	ubt_attach;
@@ -792,6 +798,13 @@
 	/* Claim second interface belonging to the Bluetooth part */
 	usbd_set_parent_iface(uaa->device, iface_index[1], uaa->info.bIfaceIndex);
 
+	/*
+	 * NextBSD: publish the controller as an IOBluetoothHostController
+	 * registry entry, now that its netgraph node is named and its
+	 * transfers are set up (nextbsd-kernel-extensions#27).
+	 */
+	ubt_ioreg_publish(dev);
+
 	return (0); /* success */
 
 detach:
@@ -811,6 +824,12 @@
 	struct ubt_softc	*sc = device_get_softc(dev);
 	node_p			node = sc->sc_node;
 
+	/*
+	 * NextBSD: retire the controller's IOBluetoothHostController entry
+	 * before its netgraph node goes (nextbsd-kernel-extensions#27).
+	 */
+	ubt_ioreg_retire(dev);
+
 	/* Destroy Netgraph node */
 	if (node != NULL) {
 		sc->sc_node = NULL;
